--[[
  Runes, with the svelte-aly ingot. `$state` makes a value that changes,
  and `$derived` makes a value that other values give. Read and write
  them as plain names; the ingot writes `.value` for each one.

  A markup hole that reads a rune binds to it, so the property follows
  each change.
]]

<script>
  local count = $state(0)
  const doubled = $derived(count * 2)
</script>

<ScreenGui ResetOnSpawn={false}>
  <TextButton Size={new UDim2(0, 320, 0, 48)} Activated={function() count += 1 end}>
    Clicked {count} times, doubled {doubled}
  </TextButton>
</ScreenGui>

<!--
  The rules:

  - `local name = $state(value)` and `const name = $derived(expr)`. The ingot
    writes each one as `local` or `const`.
  - A `$derived` value runs again only after a value that it reads
    changes. Code cannot write it.
  - Write a state with `=` or `+=`. A change in place, such as
    `items:push(x)`, runs nothing: assign the state again after it.
-->
